1783615818277013	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExqgM		item.comment	bn-zge	{"body":"Investigated: bn-1bn columnar codec (mess-index/src/columnar) emits self-describing blocks with a per-block columnar/raw flag + inline skeleton tables; sealed pointer sidecar (.pidx) is pointer-only. mess-store owns the DictRegistered registry (mess-index cannot dep on mess-store — reverse edge). Plan: new mess-index/src/sealed/payload.rs — D6 payload-block sidecar (.pcol) with per-block 1-bit columnar/row flag + dict_id in the block index, columnar-by-default via BlockEncoder with row fallback, permanent verify-on-seal (reassemble+memcmp, typed abort), magicless zstd-dict row-fallback tier, mixed-segment point+range replay, and a DictResolver referenced-implies-registered gate. Wired into SealDriver."}	blake3:241uhiWTmUJA6gzCrnXGAuGstnUaVJOMx-7nJYJ9cXM
1783616332789897	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExqwM		item.comment	bn-2ug	{"body":"Retention-blocking rule implemented in mess-index (crates/mess-index/src/sealed/retention.rs): pure segment_retention_decision(spans, live, anchors) plus decide_segment/spans_for_segment wiring adapter over SealedSegmentIndex (added stream_ids()/stream_range() accessors). Placement: mess-index is the only crate that already has per-stream frame-range data for a sealed segment and depends on mess-log (so it consumes real SnapshotAnchor directly). No retention executor exists yet in the codebase, so this is exposed as the documented pre-deletion gate. 4 required test shapes + 2 extras, all green; mess-index/mess-log/mess-store suites and clippy clean so far."}	blake3:qQwk3RnEsIbqKuP2Q4wMRangsK1sRv0O0WK3BPsg62I
1783616467325465	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrAM		item.comment	bn-vy3	{"body":"fold_version enforcement wired: added SnapshotMetrics.invalidated() deploy counter on EventStore; load_cached now distinguishes stale-fold (Invalidated) from ordinary miss, rebuilds by full replay, counts once, and REPLACES the stale snapshot with a fresh one stamped at the current fold_version (persist_snapshot reuses the rebuilt state, no double replay). Versioned fjall ref codec (REF_FORMAT_V1 tag) so legacy/untagged/garbled records decode as unknown -> self-heal. Tests: tests/fold_version_deploy.rs (mock deploy story a/b/c + clone-shared metric), fjall persisted round-trip + back-compat unit test. Running full suite + clippy."}	blake3:xBlTi1IgIhfU1V8obFuc8Y1Mv3Zs9ofKG6tF6HDpeIU
1783616541559398	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrQM		item.comment	bn-zge	{"body":"Done. New crates/mess-index/src/sealed/payload.rs: D6 payload-block sidecar (.pcol) — columnar-by-default via BlockEncoder, row fallback wired through the codec's decision, per-block 1-bit columnar/row flag + dict_id in the block index. PERMANENT verify-on-seal (reassemble every block through the read path + memcmp vs source; typed VerifyMismatch aborts — tested via injected source-corruption AND a corrupted stored block). Magicless zstd-dict row-fallback tier (16 KiB dicts, experimental zstd feature). referenced-implies-registered gate (DictResolver). Mixed-segment point+range replay. Wired into SealDriver::seal_payload (.pcol sibling of .pidx, crash-atomic write). 1M-event bench (release, mixed corpus): 8.86 B/event (3.92x), 722/7813 row-fallback blocks, replay 9.25 M ev/s, point read 6.2 us, seal+verify 1.34 M ev/s. mess-index 76 + mess-log 115 suites green, clippy -D warnings clean."}	blake3:31xlPLRKGDXgCB7RiiOppnSuoLOagUIttgDiQHwnops
1783617154380026	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrgM		item.comment	bn-zge	{"body":"Fixing blocking pipeline-wiring gap: adding payloads to SealInput, emitting .pcol from SealDriver::seal (so BackgroundSealer::run produces it in a real seal), attaching SealedPayloadIndex to SealedSegmentIndex (open() re-attaches sibling .pcol), and routing ReplaySet reads through .pcol (payload_at + payload_scan across mixed segments). Wiring mess-store seal_active to feed real payloads."}	blake3:X8quX8xNGj1aCgl-X7BxRj-XWu2in3e_Cq6A926J2is
1783617205709452	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrwM		item.comment	bn-meo	{"body":"Two fuzz crates stood up (crates/mess-index/fuzz: fuzz_reassemble_block; crates/mess-core/fuzz: fuzz_upcast_stored_event), each its own [workspace] following crates/mess-log/fuzz's pattern, with gen_corpus seeders. Both targets found and fixed real root-cause bugs within seconds of first run: (1) mess-index columnar decode_raw only validated the LAST offset in the raw-fallback offset table, so a non-monotonic/huge interior offset panicked slicing the buffer -- fixed by validating all offsets are non-decreasing. (2) mess-index per-column block decode had no aggregate cap across all columns' ulen fields (only each column individually was capped at 64MiB), so many small compressed columns each claiming ~64MiB could force terabytes of allocation from a tiny input -- fixed with a running-sum cap during directory parsing (CodecError::TotalUlenExceeded). (3) mess-core's msgpack decode had no nesting-depth guard, so an unknown/extra map field with a few hundred thousand levels of array nesting stack-overflowed serde's default field-skip (SIGABRT, uncatchable) -- fixed with an iterative (non-recursive) pre-walk depth check (check_msgpack_depth, MAX_MSGPACK_DEPTH=64) before handing bytes to rmp_serde. (4) the example TripCompletedV2->V3 Upcast's unit conversion panicked on integer overflow for an adversarial old-version field value -- fixed with saturating_mul. All four have regression unit tests. Running the required >=10min bounded fuzz campaigns now."}	blake3:MZKEG-sOXo7wR4tH-wL7BNSHSmTBMOqGUeKa9Spz03A
1783619312253386	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsAM		item.comment	bn-zge	{"body":"Fixed the blocking pipeline-wiring gap at root cause. Commit 2ad70bb: SealInput.payloads (optional, stored/global order); SealDriver::seal (and thus BackgroundSealer::run) now emits the .pcol payload sidecar + attaches SealedPayloadIndex to the installed segment when payloads present, running the permanent verify-on-seal (typed abort on mismatch). SealedSegmentIndex carries the payload index; open() re-attaches the sibling .pcol. ReplaySet now consumes .pcol: payload_at (global point read) + payload_scan (global-order replay across mixed columnar+row-fallback segments). mess-store seal_active feeds real payloads so a real seal produces .pcol. New tests: seal_emits_and_attaches_pcol_when_payloads_present, background_sealer_emits_pcol, seal_without_payloads_emits_no_pcol, payload_scan_reassembles_mixed_segments_in_global_order, payload_scan_requires_every_segment_to_have_a_pcol. Gates: mess-index full suite green (81 lib + integration), mess-log 115 green, clippy -D warnings clean on mess-index and mess-store; mess-store suite green so far (60+ incl. sealed-read-path + registry)."}	blake3:WNcvQXenRzySpBIX8_am0t4O7yebH5mNIgy9wd8n9so
1783619634160424	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsQM		item.create	bn-7t1	{"description":"Filed bn-rah2 in ~/src/maw (2026-07-09): 'ws merge --destroy' on 1.0.0-pre.10 silently reset sibling workspaces' HEADs to base, leaving reviewed commits dangling and work uncommitted in the tree. Recovery: verify tree vs lost commit (git diff <hash>), re-commit, sync. Until fixed: after EVERY merge, check remaining workspaces' HEADs before syncing, and never run ws undo/checkout on 'unexplained' uncommitted changes in a sibling. Check #maw for maw-dev's response; close when fixed upstream + verified here.","kind":"task","labels":["tracking"],"title":"[tracking] maw bn-rah2: merge resets sibling workspace branch pointers (pre.10 regression)"}	blake3:2q26rY-VUfhRw8BTF4w9MisiH54CPdXmWmf3BnENgjI
