1783657293382906	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExkAQ		item.comment	bn-1fo	{"body":"Starting bn-1fo: scoped the LogEngine Backend API (head/read_stream/read_global/append_batch + seal_active/total_events/sealed_segment_count) and the proven mess-log sigkill_child harness pattern. Building crates/mess-soak: in-process deterministic driver (drop-and-reopen crashes, full shadow model, all probes) for the CI smoke, plus a forked soak-child + parent SIGKILL reconciliation for the faithful nightly crash. Design decision on crash mode to be documented in README."}	blake3:KKKu5YrRHVTrOvYejFARUP004GN3HX3MPFtHVAal-8A
1783658148571373	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExkQQ		item.comment	bn-1fo	{"body":"Implemented crates/mess-soak: lib (config/prng+Zipf/shadow/probe/metrics/resource/driver) + mess-soak bin + soak-child bin + smoke tests + README. Crash-mode decision: default drop-and-reopen (in-process, deterministic, full shadow, drives all probes across restart -> used by CI smoke); --crash-mode sigkill forks soak-child under Durability::Os, SIGKILLs it mid-flight, reconciles recovery against the child's ack ledger (faithful 'no destructors ran' crash) -> nightly. Verified: 28 lib unit tests green (each probe fires on injected violation); smoke green with 3 crash cycles + all probes exercised; sigkill binary ran 4 real kill/recover rounds reconciling 678 acked events densely, zero violations; seal churn confirmed (sealed segments -> cold ReplaySet read path exercised); tmpfs --dir refused; clippy -D warnings clean. Committing."}	blake3:MpbbYdcVXTOgjDcYTw5MV0SYm4hVNxc2qhh3m9F4Td8
1783658326062267	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExkgQ		item.comment	bn-1hl	{"body":"D10 experiments done (bn-1hl): spikes/perfect_hash_directory (HashMap vs sorted/binary-search vs hand-rolled FKS MPH vs fjall, 1k/100k/1M streams) -> DECLINE the MPH, current HashMap wins on latency + memory at every size. spikes/odsync_probe (group-commit-shaped O_DSYNC vs fdatasync, 4-64KiB) -> round-4's 2.3-4.4x NOT reproduced on this run (host was heavily contended: load avg ~8, 22GiB swap in use; cross-checked against perf_group_commit's own unmodified round-4 harness, which shows the same collapse right now) -- reported as confounded, not contradicted, re-run-on-quiet-host left open. Startup device-capability probe designed as code (spikes/odsync_probe/src/probe.rs: opt-in gated, bandwidth-trap lying-device heuristic, documented FUA caveat), not wired into production. docs/perf/experiments-d10.md ties both verdicts together. No production crate touched; both clippy-clean. Commit 7cc2f478."}	blake3:PEQ0U0w3HwphqpLMm8sDsuUulATWxenoy_cFn-NOnIU
1783658367084331	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExkwQ		item.comment	bn-e2y	{"body":"Runtime metrics landed: new lock-free metrics core in mess-log (metrics.rs) — HdrHistogram-style log-scale LatencyHistogram (p50/p95/p99, <=~6% rel error), Counter, and a latching rate-limited DegradationAlarm (default 50ms, configurable). Committer instrumented at the fdatasync barrier site (mandatory doc03 s2.6): fsync latency histogram + degradation flag + throughput counters (groups/batches/events/bytes), exposed via Committer::metrics() and LogEngine::metrics()->EngineMetrics (adds cache hit/miss, sealed count, watermark for SUB9 lag, active-segment age). mess inspect gains an offline metrics section (segment sizes/ages/counts) + an advisory documenting the in-process/offline split. Tests: histogram percentiles over uniform+bimodal distributions, alarm latch, committer throughput+degradation-flag-fires (threshold-0 injection), engine metrics under durable workload, inspect offline section. All of mess-log/mess-store/mess-cli suites green; clippy -D warnings clean on all three. Buffered-append hot-path overhead measured (same-machine A/B): ~1.3%, inside the ~4% noise band — trivial."}	blake3:nK8ldPGS4YOWQUlv8O_BnD0mxT5wRSC4xg8LGslDlV8
1783659771882328	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExlAQ		item.comment	bn-e2y	{"body":"Review fixes (all 3 blocking): (1) SCOPE 2 seal/sidecar fsync now instrumented — write_durable's temp-file + directory fsyncs (mess-index driver.rs) are timed into a LatencyHistogram AND fed a latching seal-fsync DegradationAlarm via a new shared SealMetrics sink, so a near-full-SSD stall on the seal barrier surfaces exactly like the commit barrier. (2) SCOPE 2 seal durations — SealDriver::seal now times roll->installed into seal_duration + a seals counter, surfaced in EngineMetrics.{seal_fsync,seal_fsync_degraded,seal_duration,seals}. (3) SCOPE 5 — block cache is now enable-able via EngineOptions.block_cache_budget_bytes (default 64 MiB, on) instead of hardwired disabled(); new test cache_and_seal_metrics_move_under_workload seals then re-reads a sealed stream, proving cache miss->hit AND seal duration/fsync move under load. Gates: clippy -D warnings clean (mess-index/log/store/cli); full suites green."}	blake3:Z26cpRbY_8pZwus3VhqV7wjemvGP7eBy2Kywl50if4E
1783660150812091	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExlQQ		item.comment	bn-fyo	{"body":"Diagnosed and fixed. Root cause was two-layer: (1) the harness's Vec-push symbolic-length batch builder + one shared #[kani::unwind(6)] across all nested loops (varint_round_trips itself had NO unwind bound at all and also ran away past 1000 iterations when tested standalone -- confirmed independently). (2) Deeper finding via ablation: decode_ptr_block's own 'for _ in 1..n' loop (n read back from a Vec<u8> that depends on symbolic input) is fundamentally intractable for CBMC here -- confirmed decode blows up to >3GB RSS within ~10s even with a single 2-valued symbolic selector, while encode_ptr_block alone and the raw varint fns stay fast (~2s) regardless of domain width. Every redesign attempted (discretized selectors, narrow LEB128-boundary windows, fixed-size arrays) still hit this once decode touched symbolic bytes. Also found and fixed a real bug this surfaced: decode_ptr_block had no bound on n before Vec::with_capacity(n) -- a corrupted/adversarial sidecar could abort the process, violating the module's own 'never a panic' contract; fixed with a data-derived bound (n <= block.len()). Final state: kept varint_round_trips as the one real Kani proof (full u64 domain, ~2s); the round-trip properties are now covered by randomized tests (mess-index's existing seeded-xorshift convention, no proptest dep) -- full header domain, all LEB128 width boundaries, 2..=8-batch chains with strict-ordering checks. Full default 'cargo kani -p mess-index' now completes in ~2s total. cargo test -p mess-index and clippy both green."}	blake3:xDlkcv-aw53O6vsPjkQb4e0_avtyWxo6Bh75_Mh3I8w
1783661722191551	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExlgQ		item.move	bn-e2y	{"state":"done"}	blake3:l402unNSOsN_ibPWlyj33Ogu37EfIdOUsLlHKXhGXJ4
1783661722223590	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExlwQ		item.move	bn-1fo	{"state":"done"}	blake3:0GSLwAYOuNfWJDOZYrwvQ6L65lZUt_abibzxQFzW3yM
