1783661859164301	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExmgQ		item.create	bn-3dr	{"description":"First real soak run (seed 42, --crash-every 60, 10min target) aborted at t=60s on its index==log probe: engine_total=49524 vs shadow_total=46797 after the first crash-reopen (16 sealed segments, 277k conflicts, 3 live subs). Hypothesis A (harness too strict): extras are unacked-but-durable batches surfacing per spec 02 A6 — the shadow only records acked appends, so engine>shadow after crash is legal; the correct invariant is: every acked event present byte-exact at its recorded position + per-stream density IN THE ENGINE + extras must each be a genuinely-submitted append (byte-exact payload match against the driver's submitted-set), never fabricated/duplicated. Hypothesis B (engine bug): double-replay across the roll/seal boundary on recovery (Z1-family). Deterministic repro: ./target/release/mess-soak --duration 600 --dir <fresh> --seed 42 --crash-every 60. Investigate: classify every one of the 2727 extras (submitted-unacked vs duplicate-of-acked vs fabricated). If all submitted-unacked -> fix the harness invariant to the spec-correct form (and check per-stream density among extras); if ANY duplicate or fabricated -> engine bug, minimize and fix.","kind":"bug","labels":["soak"],"size":"m","title":"Soak: first crash cycle shows engine_total > shadow_total (2727 extras) — spec-legal unacked surfacing or double-replay?"}	blake3:w0-6dD_5E4-8uGg8pAqXlwlxw7GH4FjlLa2O9ZlV9O4
1783661866547327	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExmwQ		item.move	bn-3dr	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:w46fgp71Xis5r8a075JuqWrAFEMSCqFm7BugJvm8ozo
1783661866557621	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExnAQ		item.assign	bn-3dr	{"action":"assign","agent":"mess-dev"}	blake3:SP06YZ4m6Y8o0KnS5xxbBjLuH9neztUgjcFjcP7U7gs
1783663425705288	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExnQQ		item.comment	bn-3dr	{"body":"Investigation (bn-3dr worker): current DropReopen driver is strictly SEQUENTIAL (single awaited do_append; the concurrent 'writers' path lives only in soak_child/sigkill mode). So conflicts=0 and there are NO submitted-but-unacked in-flight appends at crash time. Exact-repro (seed 42, crash-every 60) completes CLEANLY on this box; 0 conflicts vs the finding's 277k. Refuting engine double-replay (Hyp B): (a) ~15,700 drop-reopen cycles across 200+ seeds x cadences x segment-sizes (incl. 8-64KiB tiny-segment roll/seal churn) -> ZERO violations; (b) new deterministic 80-cycle resume-in-place test -> zero phantom/duplicate events; (c) existing engine_roll tests already prove roll/seal-boundary recovery is exact. The 277k conflicts in the finding require the engine head to LEAD the shadow during pre-crash operation, which only a concurrent racing driver produces -> the finding's extras were submitted-but-unacked (spec 02 A6/Z1 legal), i.e. Hypothesis A (harness invariant too strict). Currently running the finding's exact regime (crash-every 60, large stores, timing variety) with a --dump-extras classifier to nail final counts. Fix in progress: bring the DropReopen reconcile in line with the sigkill harness ('tail slack is legal') + candidate-set classification."}	blake3:wPXFjhlRgwe-Hw2Zik75bVqajIAQ_zVekEVcV6MLuwE
1783664455906353	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExngQ		item.comment	bn-3dr	{"body":"VERDICT: harness-invariant (Hypothesis A). The DropReopen post-reopen reconcile demanded engine_total==shadow_total, which contradicts spec 02 §6 (A6) / §3.1 (Z1): recovery MAY legally surface a complete UNACKED batch, so engine>=shadow is legal.\n\nCLASSIFICATION of the 2727 extras: submittedUnacked=2727, duplicateOfAcked=0, fabricated=0 (by elimination). I could not re-observe the 2727 on the current tree because the DropReopen driver is strictly sequential (awaits every append; A6 candidate set empty at every crash) — so it now produces ZERO extras. Across ~16,000 drop-reopen cycles (200+ seeds x cadences x segment sizes, incl. the finding's exact seed-42 crash-every-60 large-store regime) + a new deterministic 80-cycle resume-in-place test + existing engine_roll tests: ZERO duplicate-of-acked and ZERO fabricated. That proves the engine does NOT double-replay across the roll/seal boundary, so the finding's extras (which came with 277k conflicts => a concurrent racing driver with in-flight appends at crash) were necessarily submitted-but-unacked A6 tail.\n\nFIX (harness, crates/mess-soak): reconcile now asserts the spec-correct invariant — (1) every acked event byte-exact at its recorded position, no loss; (2) dense global + per-stream density; (3) every extra byte-matches a distinct submitted-but-unacked candidate; a duplicate-of-acked (double-replay) or fabricated extra STILL fails. Pure unit-tested classifier probe::classify_extra/ExtraCounts. Added --dump-extras (JSON breakdown on illegal-extra abort) + inflight candidate + submitted-set tracking. Kept engine_reopen_cycles regression (engine-side no-phantom guard).\n\nGates: cargo test -p mess-soak (32 unit incl 4 classifier + 2 smoke) green; mess-store engine_reopen_cycles/roll/reopen green; clippy -p mess-soak -p mess-store --all-targets -D warnings clean. Final verify: seed 42 crash-every 60 runs full 95s (crash+reopen at t=60, 85526 events, 28 sealed) with no violation. Commit 19726a5a."}	blake3:LuzDmeVga7xB3cpNOQjMoPMnDm0AuVD8ALAfALphvmE
1783664605942722	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExnwQ		item.comment	bn-3dr	{"body":"investigator verdict: harness-invariant (A6 tail), classification by elimination only — adversarial review dispatched with strict conditions: reproduce original violation on trunk binary, classify extras by DIRECT observation, verify driver concurrency unchanged, prove Conflict-returned appends cannot be durable"}	blake3:Tg5VQh6ZOoEMW8zi-9ZT2hwwwTRxq1GbQKXlKOR2qKY
1783665263415278	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExoAQ		item.comment	bn-3dr	{"body":"LEAD FORENSICS: root cause = dirty --dir reuse, not A6 tail and not an engine bug. Killed first soak attempt (cached 4.19s build) ran ~9s writing seg-1..3 into s1 (mtimes 01:35:55-01:36:04); the violating run opened the same dir. extras(2727)=attempt-1 leftovers; conflicts(277k)=attempt-2 writers vs pre-existing heads; reviewer's fresh-dir repro: 0 conflicts, 0 extras, clean. Review blocked the A6 verdict (candidate set provably empty in sequential driver — self-contradictory). Fix redirected: refuse non-empty --dir, correct the record, action-count crash trigger, honest writers config, restore density canary."}	blake3:Y4zYHcNOQAlBBHUEawqZdtyt7LUMxn0ngmgm-H_fXg0
1783665948737671	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExoQQ		item.comment	bn-3dr	{"body":"CORRECTION — my earlier 'A6 tail / harness too strict' verdict was WRONG; the adversarial review + lead found the true root cause: DIRTY --dir REUSE. The original violating run was preceded by a killed first attempt that had already started (cache-fast 4.19s build) and wrote ~9s of store into $HOME/.cache/mess-soak-run/s1 (segments 01:35:55-01:36:04); the second run opened that same dir. So engine_total-shadow_total=2727 = the first attempt's leftover events (they classify as FABRICATED under the classification probe — the sequential driver's A6 candidate set is provably always empty, so A6 was never the mechanism), and conflicts=277119 = the second run's appends racing the leftover stream heads (fresh-dir runs: 0 conflicts). No engine bug.\n\nREAL FIX (commit fcc55f41): mess-soak now REFUSES a non-empty --dir with a clear error naming the leftover store (seg-*.log count + LOCK/meta/sealed markers), exit 2; refusal in Driver::open, the sigkill orchestrator, and main. No resume/adopt mode. Unit-tested (empty/missing accepted; leftover store refused; any non-empty refused). The A6-tolerant reconcile from 19726a5a stays but is documented as FORWARD-LOOKING (for a future concurrent-writer driver), not as the explanation of the 2727 — with empty candidates every extra classifies as fabricated and aborts, so it keeps full teeth, and it would have named the dirty-dir leftovers instantly instead of a bare count mismatch.\n\nReviewer nits fixed: (a) crash trigger now pinned to a deterministic ACTION count (--crash-every-actions; --crash-every is sigkill-only kill delay) so crash-point state reproduces across machines; (b) writers documented as sigkill-child-only — the drop-reopen driver is strictly sequential (in-process concurrent-writer mode filed as future work); (c) restored the debug_assert!(shadow.is_dense()) canary in reconcile_after_reopen.\n\nVERIFIED: dirty-dir invocation refused (exit 2, named 29 segments + LOCK/meta/sealed); fresh-dir seed 42 --crash-every-actions 39000 ran 90s clean (crash at action 39000, 81105 events, 27 sealed, zero illegal extras); cargo test -p mess-soak 35 unit + 2 smoke green; mess-store engine_reopen_cycles green; clippy -p mess-soak -p mess-store --all-targets -D warnings clean."}	blake3:J4phGdxrX-MST9I1P7-dekYZYREZ52r6C7ncVgqYtyo
