1783666531331475	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrwQ		item.comment	bn-h8a	{"body":"Fixed all 7 mess_ecs clippy lints (unused PhantomData import, non-canonical PartialOrd/Ord on StrPos, 5x mismatched-lifetime-syntax/elidable-lifetime sites). Fixing mess_ecs uncovered a second, previously-masked issue: crates/mess's facade re-export of the now-clean-but-still-#![deprecated] mess_ecs triggered a deprecated-use error under -D warnings once mess_ecs itself stopped failing to compile first. Added #[allow(deprecated)] there (2 lines) to reach a fully clean workspace-wide clippy. cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings is now fully clean (exit 0); cargo test -p mess_ecs: 17/17 pass. Commit f717e482."}	blake3:k5WW-aH6ro6RRCAqgQxkkU1rV25Fgm7HAMAQ-MMVKj4
1783667231835435	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsAQ		item.comment	bn-2ln	{"body":"Implemented online backup+restore (bn-2ln): docs/spec/07-backup.md defines the consistent cut (sealed segments whole + active prefix to durable watermark + BACKUP_MANIFEST written last; torn tail beyond watermark harmless). mess-cli: backup.rs (compute_cut, temp+rename, incremental via size+CRC, manifest last), restore.rs (refuses non-empty target + torn/absent manifest, copies back, runs verify --full, checks recovered watermark), lease.rs (TTL-expiring retention lease so a crashed backup cannot leak the pin). mess-index retention: added BackupLease + lease_holds + segment_deletable so the bn-2ug decision function is lease-aware; retention explain surfaces lease-hold blockers. Key correction: the meta/ name interner (bn-20b/bn-150) is durable source-of-truth NOT rebuildable from the log, so the cut MUST include meta/. Tests: 6 mess-cli integration shapes green (live-writer backup excludes post-cut events, crash torn-tail excluded, incremental copies only new segments, torn-backup refused, non-empty target refused, lease blocks then releases) + 3 lease unit + 3 index lease unit. clippy clean."}	blake3:KgNVqyOdvnseUClVcu1AnwhoKJOnn47WA_Jh39H-AUc
1783667433252030	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsQQ		item.comment	bn-2za	{"body":"Implemented RS parity sidecar (.par) + verify --repair. New module mess-index/src/sealed/parity.rs (reed-solomon-simd 3.1.0, MIT AND BSD-3-Clause). Default 4KiB shards, 16+1 per group = 6.348% overhead (6.25% parity + ~0.1% per-shard CRC table). Deterministic (no timestamps). Seal-time write wired into the background roll-sealer, OFF by default via EngineOptions.parity. verify --repair localizes damaged blocks by per-shard CRC, RS-reconstructs, then RE-VERIFIES the reconstructed image against batch CRCs + fold chain BEFORE writing, keeps damaged original as .damaged-<ts>, reports exact repaired blocks. Refuses on parity-self-corruption / beyond-tolerance / length-mismatch. Measured on full 256 MiB segment: gen 161ms (~1585 MiB/s), sidecar 17,039,412 bytes, 6.348% overhead. Tests: 9 mess-index unit + 4 mess-cli acceptance shapes + 1 mess-store seal-wiring, all green; clippy clean."}	blake3:M4CeRi5i6iFy65RqeiTh7FlgfoMo60hUG112plS012E
1783667788458938	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsgQ		item.comment	bn-3l0	{"body":"Wired fold_chain::ChainHead through the committer: opt-in ChainInit (default OFF stays byte-identical), per-stream heads materialize crypto_chain per batch, advanced only after a durable write. Engine EngineOptions.chain rehydrates heads from recovered frames on reopen. Added mess-cli/tests/chain_verify.rs (byte-identity, crash-reopen continuation + load_verified, CRC-repaired tamper caught by verify --full) and golden v4 (real on-disk chain). Overhead ~12% throughput reduction (370k->325k ev/s) under Process durability. clippy clean; mess-log + mess-cli suites green; mess-store running."}	blake3:495GPAoJK3EvlOkVcWT0Y_ArHLV6FtjYiQRAJ464aW4
1783668280599371	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExswQ		item.comment	bn-3l0	{"body":"Committed d73b22a1. All acceptance green: mess-log (17+ test binaries ok), mess-store (17 ok blocks incl snapshot_plus_tail with MESS_SNAPSHOT_LAW_ITERS=50), mess-cli (golden v3+v4, chain_verify x3) all pass; clippy -D warnings clean on all three crates. Five test shapes: (1) byte-identity chain-off, (2) chain-on materialize+verify, (3) crash-reopen continuation + load_verified, (4) CRC-repaired tamper caught by verify --full, (5) golden v4 with real on-disk chain. Overhead ~12% (Process durability, upper bound; fsync modes amortize it)."}	blake3:UE_WQMg_A6hSTKO7c5p4uoz9yeQL5sRfSTEzYrWnXdA
