1783709819770307	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6gQ		item.move	bn-1mw	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:46f2i8z8T9mXVzY-txDhIab_7OvIEA8BDZfCyDkQLHg
1783709819795272	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6wQ		item.assign	bn-1mw	{"action":"assign","agent":"mess-dev"}	blake3:cTse-CET4bXugyKfuaSon_D0meDwj7gW1oFVo3CuNj8
1783711365674954	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx7AQ		item.comment	bn-1mw	{"body":"Implemented: social-seed bin (src/seed.rs generator, deterministic StdRng, guard_fresh_dir mirroring mess-soak's UX) producing 50 users / 88 follows / 500 posts / 800 likes / 30 deletes / 20 unfollows in ~8.5s (well under 60s budget) via real WriteOps/EventStore::command calls only. Wired social-web --dir to a real EventStore<LogEngine> + Projections<LogEngine> (new src/store_backend.rs for the DynRead/DynWrite orphan-rule-constrained impls; Projections::directory() added to populate the handle<->Id side table at boot). Verified end-to-end: seeded, served, curled / and /u/<handle> (real seeded HTML back), killed+restarted the server and diffed the HTML byte-for-byte (identical — the rebuild-from-log party trick), ran mess doctor/inspect/verify --full/backup/restore against the real seeded store (all real trimmed output pasted into the new README), and confirmed a restored-from-backup store serves byte-identical pages too. Added just demo (seed --force && serve). README.md rewrite for examples/social with the domain ASCII diagram, quickstart, rebuild trick, and full ops tour + dogfood findings (inspect's text format drops dir/lock/registry/stream_heads since Report::to_text() never renders Report::extra; stream_heads has no pagination/name resolution; doctor's fold-version check degrades under a live writer's fjall lock). Gates green: cargo test -p social (56 tests), clippy -p social --all-targets -D warnings, cargo check --workspace."}	blake3:s6zzd0jXlA_ozV83ME4T2YuO-q4LUvNaAWzWbpDu19I
1783712035317587	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx7QQ		item.create	bn-cxr	{"description":"With TMPDIR pointed at a persistent dir ($HOME/.cache/mess-test-tmp, required because /tmp is quota-limited tmpfs and real-fs suites fallocate 256MiB segments), leaked temp store dirs accumulated to 302GB / 737 dirs in two days. Leak paths: (1) crash/SIGKILL harness tests kill children by design — TempDir::drop never runs; (2) failed/aborted runs; (3) nothing sweeps ~/.cache (unlike tmpfs). Fix: a mess-testkit helper (used by all real-fs suites incl. crash harnesses + social tests) that creates temp stores under <TMPDIR>/mess-tests/<name>-<pid>-... AND at init sweeps sibling dirs older than 24h (age by mtime, best-effort, never fails the test). Alternative/addition: a 'just clean-test-tmp' recipe + a line in the testing docs. Acceptance: run a SIGKILL-harness suite twice; the second run removes the first run's leaked dirs; normal concurrent runs never delete each other's live dirs (age threshold + pid-liveness check).","kind":"task","labels":["dx"],"size":"s","title":"Test temp hygiene: real-fs suites leak 256MiB store dirs under TMPDIR (302GB accumulated) — add self-sweeping helper"}	blake3:iwJWKvl8T5tVTb11zEH9xdTvqMHJduvTBSrSwCG7ix4
1783712228431757	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx7gQ		item.move	bn-1mw	{"state":"done"}	blake3:kG2HAbCQbLIpuJZ_ydJL6efMArArza8wQ-EWU6XI-zI
1783713806913749	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx7wQ		item.move	bn-j9u	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:4f7KAWOgj91i9Od1cGDXiH5se3wdnM_hSEYV1hZDp3w
1783713806920979	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx8AQ		item.assign	bn-j9u	{"action":"assign","agent":"mess-dev"}	blake3:UEHoLLBus4RuKz1P5VLHDtVwjDw37oIIiS8LwcFd130
1783713844761231	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx8QQ		item.create	bn-3mu	{"description":"THE headline dogfood finding (bn-2xl): EventStore exposes no subscription/live-tail — only Backend::read_global(after,limit) via store.backend(). mess-log's D11 catch-up->live runtime (subscription.rs, ReadView/Watermark) is not wired to EventStore, so every app read model hand-rolls a polling adapter (social's projections poll at 1ms) with no commit notification to await — wait_for latency is poll-bounded, not event-bounded. Proposed (worker sketch): EventStore::subscribe(from: Option<u64>) -> impl Stream<Item=StoredRecord> (or Subscription handle with async next_batch()) backed by the engine watermark, plus store-level watermark()/await_past(pos). Evidence: examples/social/src/projections.rs's polling adapter and its module docs.","kind":"task","labels":["dx","dogfood"],"size":"m","title":"EventStore: app-facing subscription API (catch-up -> live tail)"}	blake3:_bYqEW3VTeTWp3lzJa2PgLFTFlBROTL4Dd3DXy2WBjg
1783713844928979	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx8gQ		item.create	bn-2i3	{"description":"bn-154: Decide sees only folded state, never the stream id it was loaded from, so self-referential invariants force commands to restate the actor (social's Follow carries follower: Id that the stream key already implies — divergence between them is representable and must not be). Options: pass stream id into decide (context param), an Aggregate::stream_id accessor set at load, or bless the actor-field convention in docs. Evidence: examples/social/src/domain/user.rs Follow + its doc comment.","kind":"task","labels":["dx","dogfood"],"size":"s","title":"Decide: expose the stream id (or standardize actor convention)"}	blake3:q9ydDzO2YbAzE9tqf-w-qds7_UamgUgo99PdF-M8DeQ
1783713845091657	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx8wQ		item.create	bn-3c6	{"description":"Found twice (bn-154, bn-2xl): Id is Hash but not Ord — set-valued aggregate state and every projection index must be HashSet/HashMap; ordered feed indices via BTreeMap impossible; HashSet iteration nondeterminism also bit the seed generator (bn-1mw). Any future fold-certificate hashing of aggregate state will need ordered (or order-independent) iteration. Add Ord/PartialOrd to Id.","kind":"task","labels":["dx","dogfood"],"size":"xs","title":"ident::Id: implement Ord (BTree indices, deterministic iteration)"}	blake3:x965myUlncydpGaW4Vsli-HoX3c7uKY0yFTjizP8AOE
1783713845254220	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9AQ		item.create	bn-19b	{"description":"bn-2xl: read_global yields stream_id as opaque String; projections must string-prefix-match 'user-'/'post-' and Id::from_str the suffix to route events, with a parse-can-fail path. Expose a typed category discriminator (or the engine's interned category id + name) on StoredRecord so multi-aggregate consumers dispatch without string surgery. Evidence: examples/social/src/projections.rs apply_record.","kind":"task","labels":["dx","dogfood"],"size":"s","title":"StoredRecord: typed stream/category routing (kill stringly-typed prefix dispatch)"}	blake3:efSZOuROD0NJmku24vg2iCfQTGq9EdoO35kSp0NQvXg
1783713865043463	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9QQ		item.create	bn-3uu	{"description":"bn-2xl: silent-skip on decode/Id-parse failure is the right liveness policy for a projection modeling a slice of the log, but there is no way to notice 'I skipped N records' — schema drift would be invisible. Add an anomaly counter surface (projection-side helper in mess-core or a metrics hook on the store read path) so operators see skips. Evidence: projections.rs apply_record silent-skip comment.","kind":"task","labels":["dx","dogfood"],"size":"xs","title":"Projection anomaly observability: surface undecodable/unroutable records"}	blake3:KCyMhaVBKY_Y-XRoAQXgQXY7DsU5i8P2I70qcoOZQFw
1783713865211551	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9gQ		item.create	bn-188	{"description":"bn-154: CommandError<R,S>'s two type params (rejection + backend error) ripple into every caller signature; social's WriteOps collapses them to a stringified enum at its seam. Provide a first-class erase/flatten helper on the store (e.g. CommandError::erased() -> CommandError<R, BoxError> or a store method returning it) so app seams don't each reinvent this. Evidence: contracts.rs WriteError.","kind":"task","labels":["dx","dogfood"],"size":"xs","title":"CommandError ergonomics: store-error erasure helper"}	blake3:_7LmaRrliFFzjMzc7E3xpPM5HiO8fUL7Xl0pvCg266M
1783713865383435	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9wQ		item.create	bn-162	{"description":"bn-1mw: 1,488 sequential EventStore::command calls (load-decide-append round trips) = ~8.5s quiet / 50-70s under contention. Fine at demo scale; a 10x seed or any bulk importer wants a pipeline (concurrent commands to distinct streams now safe under bn-1s0's per-stream gate — document that pattern) and/or a multi-command batch API. Could be docs-first: a 'bulk writes' guide showing join_all over distinct-stream commands, measuring the win. Evidence: seed.rs timing note.","kind":"task","labels":["dx","dogfood"],"size":"s","title":"Store write throughput: batching/pipelining primitive for bulk producers"}	blake3:fAKJYJRQXGd2b5LadsmfpjJgfcKsNwAFqX3DUOm_baQ
1783713865548436	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-AQ		item.create	bn-1yz	{"description":"bn-1mw, reviewer-confirmed: (1) piped/agent-default text format renders only findings + the named collection, never Report::extra — where inspect puts dir/lock/metrics/registry/stream_heads — so plain 'mess inspect <dir>' on a 550-stream app store prints one JSON blob and nothing else (doctor's content lives in findings and IS text-visible: inconsistent). (2) --format pretty stream_heads has no truncation/pagination and entries are {stream_id: <interned int>, name: null} — impossible to correlate user-<Id>/post-<Id> without out-of-band lookup; --stream requires already knowing the number. Resolve names via the interner tables. (3) Reviewer found field-name drift between live-writer-locked and offline runs (registry_source/stream_heads vs registry/stream_names) — output schema should be lock-state-independent. Evidence: examples/social README ops-tour + bn-1mw review.","kind":"task","labels":["cli","dogfood"],"size":"s","title":"mess inspect: text format drops Report::extra; stream_heads unusable at app scale; field-name stability"}	blake3:WIbOgjrvZi459o5jnqOl7fM-_eqxqgu8GL7irTracyk
1783713885915169	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-QQ		item.create	bn-ve0	{"description":"bn-1mw: doctor's fold-version check needs the fjall meta store, which a live writer holds exclusively; against a running app it degrades to 'could not read: FjallError: Locked' (info severity — correct behavior, surprising UX). Document the live-probe caveat in doctor's help/README, and investigate a read-only fjall open (or snapshot-based read) so the check works against live stores. Evidence: examples/social README ops-tour.","kind":"task","labels":["cli","dogfood"],"size":"xs","title":"mess doctor: live-writer stores degrade fold-version check (fjall lock) — document + read-only fallback"}	blake3:pVWfvwkx4habNLajpcBIhLW_4lZsB-3AmadHf1fCoKU
1783713886079880	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-gQ		item.create	bn-3mc	{"description":"bn-13l: repo rustfmt.toml has nightly-only options, so stable 'cargo fmt --check' flags already-committed files. Either gate CI fmt on nightly explicitly (document it) or trim to stable options. Today workers avoid formatting entirely to dodge churn — that is the wrong equilibrium.","kind":"task","labels":["dx"],"size":"xs","title":"rustfmt.toml uses nightly-only options: stable cargo fmt --check reports spurious diffs"}	blake3:mEL6nm26AzaIoQVQ36T3fL_aL6yLZlSuH5tjs-_8wBc
1783713886243632	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-wQ		item.create	bn-2v0	{"description":"bn-154 documented in-crate that Decide cannot check another aggregate's existence (Follow cannot verify target is registered) and the event-sourcing answer (accept + reconcile downstream, or saga with compensating events). Promote this from example-crate doc comment to the mess-core/store docs as the blessed posture, with the social example as the worked reference. Evidence: domain/user.rs module docs.","kind":"task","labels":["docs","dogfood"],"size":"xs","title":"docs: cross-aggregate invariants posture (accept + reconcile / saga pattern)"}	blake3:HvsIDh1-mJdL85wtntPtmyKnsLhxPXQl29UgL8BlKfU
1783713886413238	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx_AQ		item.create	bn-3n7	{"description":"bn-13l follow-ups, all social-internal: (1) add + Send to ReadModels/WriteOps async-fn-in-trait so axum consumes them generically and the DynRead/DynWrite shims (store_backend.rs) can be deleted; (2) typed ids in DTOs: PostView.id as a typed PostId (not String re-parsed by handlers), author id alongside author_handle so author-only UI stops comparing handle strings; (3) ReadModels::resolve(handle)->Id (or ids in DTOs make it moot) so frontends stop maintaining side directories (Projections::directory() bootstrap becomes internal). Evidence: web/ handlers + store_backend.rs shims.","kind":"task","labels":["social"],"parent":"bn-3eh","size":"s","title":"social: contracts polish — Send bounds, typed ids in DTOs, handle resolution"}	blake3:i-NtGjRmAZug6t8XeiPP0aGZm2BS20wE1-Opov9telc
1783713900700426	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx_QQ		item.comment	bn-3eh	{"body":"DOGFOOD TRIAGE COMPLETE (bn-j9u): 19 raw findings from bn-154/bn-2xl/bn-13l/bn-1mw deduplicated into 12 bones. mess core/store: bn-3mu (EventStore subscription API — THE headline), bn-2i3 (Decide stream-id access), bn-3c6 (Id: Ord), bn-19b (typed stream routing on StoredRecord), bn-3uu (projection anomaly counter), bn-188 (CommandError erasure helper), bn-162 (bulk-write pipeline/docs). CLI: bn-1yz (inspect text/extra + stream_heads + field stability), bn-ve0 (doctor live-store fjall caveat). Repo DX: bn-3mc (rustfmt nightly options). Docs: bn-2v0 (cross-aggregate posture). Social-internal: bn-3n7 (Send bounds, typed DTO ids, handle resolution). No-action: HashSet-iteration determinism trap (documented in seed.rs where it was caught); MemBackend wiring (resolved by bn-1mw). Every bone cites its concrete social-example evidence."}	blake3:lMixG5ysFogIpjVN-6pieHQmQLkxQ7vJ0K1qDVpsdkI
