1783730214451419	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExyQU		item.create	bn-imm	{"description":"The 302GB->cleaned->349GB-again cycle: tests/projections.rs and tests/store_roundtrip.rs (and any other social real-fs test) use a hand-rolled fresh_dir() creating TempDirs directly under TMPDIR; each real store preallocates a 256MB segment and crash/abort paths leak it; ~1,362 dirs accumulated in one day of wave testing. mess-testkit sweeping_temp_dir (bn-cxr) landed but was only adopted in mess-log/mess-store crash suites. Swap social fresh_dir to the sweeping helper (namespaced under mess-tests/, 24h+pid-guarded auto-sweep). Also audit remaining hand-rolled TempDir sites across example/bench crates. Found by the bn-o9z reviewer when the full disk blocked verification.","kind":"task","labels":["dx","dogfood"],"size":"xs","title":"social tests: adopt the bn-cxr sweeping temp helper in fresh_dir (leak engine for the 349GB refill)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:pDSyzpojCptWO6yBP_szSVWHWQjAlLJdVfX6Su3gVZg
1783730214617413	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExygU		item.create	bn-tjs	{"description":"bn-o9z dogfood: the warm write path needs SnapshotStore (FjallSnapshotBackend) and the projections pump needs SubscribeBackend (bn-3mu), but FjallSnapshotBackend<B> does not forward SubscribeBackend from its wrapped B — no single backend type has both capabilities, so social runs a second EventStore over a cloned Arc-shared LogEngine (store_backend::read_handle) purely to subscribe. A trivial forwarding impl (impl<B: SubscribeBackend> SubscribeBackend for FjallSnapshotBackend<B>) collapses the two handles into one type. Evidence: examples/social/src/store_backend.rs read_handle + README Concerns.","kind":"task","labels":["dogfood","dx"],"size":"xs","title":"FjallSnapshotBackend: forward SubscribeBackend to the wrapped backend"}	blake3:o8v5TI0KsDuSU4VeWKdls230OcU1bYwFL0PLdQNBE4o
1783730214781768	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExywU		item.create	bn-3dy	{"description":"bn-o9z dogfood: doctor could not be made non-vacuous even against a snapshot-using store. Two causes: (a) command_cached only READS snapshots on cold miss and never proactively save_snapshot, so a normally-running app persists none; (b) when snapshots ARE saved, FjallSnapshotBackend writes sidecar meta (<dir>/.snapshots/meta) keyed by interim FNV stream ids while mess-cli metaread reads the engine <dir>/meta and correlates by registry stream ids — the id spaces never intersect, so the drift check can never see app snapshots. Fix direction: share the meta store or key snapshots by registry id; possibly also an optional snapshot-write policy (every N events) so real apps persist snapshots at all. Evidence: examples/social README Concerns section (bn-o9z).","kind":"task","labels":["dogfood","cli"],"size":"s","title":"doctor fold-version check vs FjallSnapshotBackend: snapshot meta id-spaces never line up (check is structurally vacuous)"}	blake3:sacnflKv8M9jKZgYczbHnQoANmDeNE20C3djOURYZOk
1783730214948026	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExzAU		item.create	bn-5iu	{"description":"bn-o9z dogfood: the seeder could not switch to Durability::Group to demonstrate fsync-coalesced pipelining (the bulk-writes guide headline 7-23x) because Durability is not re-exported from mess-store — reaching it requires depending on mess-log directly, which the example correctly refuses to do. Re-export it next to EngineOptions. Consequence documented in the social README: seed timings are Durability::Process, pipelining ratio 1.3-1.75x CPU-bound.","kind":"task","labels":["dogfood","dx"],"size":"xs","title":"mess-store: re-export Durability so apps can choose fsync mode without a mess-log dep"}	blake3:wVXw1N3hdPlxFXK3F_kGkcTSbzs-zQKzKsIO_Zz32CA
