1783736989346429	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx5QU		item.create	bn-1jg	{"description":"D10-style measurement spike, no production changes. The large-tier seed runs ~2.3ms/command (54,680 events / 126s pipelined; demo tier shows same ~2ms shape) while the hot-post bench warm path is 53us — a 40x gap. Workload difference: the seeder creates ~54k NEW streams (every command a cold miss: registry mint for a never-seen stream name, fjall snapshot lookup miss, load_cached on empty stream, FjallSnapshotBackend wrapping) vs the bench hammering one warm stream. Hypotheses to test by measurement (release profile ONLY): (1) per-new-stream registry/interning cost, (2) fjall snapshot-lookup miss cost, (3) FjallSnapshotBackend wrapper overhead vs plain LogEngine, (4) executor/pipelining overhead, (5) empty-stream load cost. Deliver: instrumented decomposition (e.g. a timing ProfilingBackend wrapper — no mess-* edits), new-stream vs existing-stream command latency at same store size, a REPORT with per-phase mean/p50/p99 attribution, and a conclusion naming the dominant cost with recommended follow-up bones. This taxes the relationship-stream model directly (millions of likes = millions of stream creations), so the answer shapes real work.","kind":"task","labels":["perf","dogfood"],"size":"s","title":"spike: profile the seeder 40x gap — per-command cost decomposition (2.3ms/cmd vs 53us warm bench)"}	blake3:QAioF9VwACj8UB793zLG5nGzpd7GXDT-cU7Ja27BjH0
